      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dandolo/{size}/1845_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-09-24T13:50:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I don't see the difference... both effects say \"The first time a [target type] would be dealt damage, redirect that damage to [card name].\"</p><p>In both cases the ambiguity arises from the meaning of the word \"a\" which can mean \"each\" or \"any\". If this card is meant to be \"each\" I think it needs errata.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:07:56.312Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
