    {
      "id": 182848,
      "name": "LewdDolphin21",
      "username": "LewdDolphin21",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lewddolphin21/{size}/1893_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-09-24T15:07:07.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I agree with Dandolo. The phrase \"a villain target other than this card\" and \"a hero target\" seem to be describing the applicable pool of targets for the card's effects to happen. It doesn't make sense to me for both cards to have different effects.</p><p>Going just straight off of words, say Tempest and Unity get targeted by attacks. Tempest is selected first, and this is the first time a hero target would be dealt damage this turn, so Wrong Time and Place should go off. The attack on Unity shouldn't get the option, because it is the second time a hero target would be dealt damage this turn.</p><p>If the intent was to have it affect each hero target individually, there should have been the word \"each\" somewhere in there.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:07:56.510Z",
